  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Promoting a Human Security Approach to Disaster Displacement, Environmental Migration and Disaster Risk Reduction in the Caribbean Region</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">In line with the dimensions and principles of the human security approach, the overall goal of Phase II of the programme is to promote adequate protection for disaster displaced persons, environmental migrants and vulnerable communities in the Caribbean Region to multiple threats through enhancing and promoting the interventions of Phase I. The JP will maintain its focus on outreach and advocacy, by seeking to enhance sustainability of project interventions through continuing the work to promote the integration of a human security approach in national and regional policies and programmes.The short- and medium-term objectives of the programme relate to an enhanced integration of the human security approach in disaster displacement, environmental migration and disaster risk reduction policies in the Caribbean. This will enable a preventive and comprehensive approach to the issues surrounding disaster displacement, environmental migration and disaster risk reduction. It will focus on the insecurities that affect the populations vulnerable to climate change and natural hazards in the wider CARICOM.</narrative>
  </description>
